WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:11.000
Nadia's first presentation at her internship goes badly. She loses her place twice.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.500
That night, one sentence plays on repeat: I am just bad at presenting.

3
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:24.800
It sounds like a fact. It is actually a full stop. Nothing comes after it.

4
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.700
A verdict about yourself leaves nothing to do next.

5
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.000
So she crosses it out.

6
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:42.000
I have not trained presenting with a method yet. Now there is a next step: rehearse twice, out loud, with a timer.

7
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The second belief is about energy. Nadia worries about the job market, the other interns, and what her supervisor thinks of her.

8
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.700
None of that moves when she pushes. Her rehearsals do. So do the questions she asks.

9
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:04.800
Energy spent inside your control compounds. Energy spent on the rest evaporates.

10
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:13.800
So she rehearses twice with a teammate and a timer, and asks him one question: where did you lose me?

11
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:21.900
Her second presentation is not perfect. It is clearly better. Ability turned out to be a variable.

12
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:28.000
Your personal audit comes next. It only works at one setting: honest.

13
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:35.300
That means no self-punishment and no self-promotion. Kind to the person, ruthless about the data.

14
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:40.200
“I am bad at X” is a full stop.

15
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:46.300
“I have not trained X with a method yet” is a to-do.

16
00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:55.200
Now it is your turn. Catch one verdict in your own self-talk today, and rewrite it as a method.
